# Milestone: v0.10.12-cat-e-activation
# Covers: determinism rule D-cross-2 — slot-change burst with 2 sync subs;
#         50 sequential obj.x = i writes; subscriber walk order is byte-stable
#         across 100x3 preset runs; D-slotchange-2 FIFO sub walk confirmed.
# blocked: no multi-preset runner mode.  The claim is byte-identical
#          output across 100 runs under each of three tunable presets, and
#          there is no directive that asks for repetition or for a preset
#          sweep -- `# tunables: <preset>` selects ONE and skips otherwise.
#          The language half works: Object.new(), slot-change subscription
#          and the sync subscriber walk are all live (see
#          reactive/slot-change/).
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: reactive-slot-change
#
# Reason:
#   Requires Object.new() T69 stdlib binding and inline subscriber dispatch.
#   The deferred-slot-change ring (spec #4 §5.4) and sync subscriber walk
#   (FIFO walk of obj.x.changed_watchers_head) were tested by
#   test_slot_change_callsites.c and test_slot_change_reentrancy.c until the
#   Phase 0 runtime-internals test cleanup; no C-level coverage today.
#
#   When active: 50 writes × 2 subs = 100 subscriber firings → 100-char log;
#   byte-identical across 100 runs under each of the 3 tunable presets.
#   Verifies D-slotchange-1 (program-order emit) + D-slotchange-2 (FIFO walk).
#
#   When v0.10.7-G ships: replace the source below with the activated
#   keyword-form variant.  The audit confirmed the C-level deferred-ring
#   drain + sync subscriber walk were tested by test_slot_change_callsites.c
#   and test_slot_change_reentrancy.c until the Phase 0 runtime-internals test
#   cleanup; no C-level coverage today.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate when v0.10.7-G T39 ships):
#   var obj = Object.new();
#   var Realm.log = "";
#   at sync (obj.x.changed?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "A";
#   at sync (obj.x.changed?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "B";
#   var i = 0;
#   while (i < 50) { obj.x = i; Realm.i = i + 1 };
#   Realm.log
#   --- expected output (100 chars: 50 repetitions of "AB") ---
#   [00000001] "ABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABAB"
